{:edb/db-before-t 783 :edb/db-after-t 784 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534096 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:51:53.324Z" 13194139534096 true] [17592186083066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277497 13194139534096 true] [17592186083066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277504 13194139534096 true] [17592186083067 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277490 13194139534096 true] [17592186083068 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277511 13194139534096 true] [17592186083789 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534096 true] [17592186083789 1100 "Find the range of the function $f(x) = \\frac{1}{3}\\csc (\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{π}{8}) - 1$." 13194139534096 false] [17592186083789 1100 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})-1.$" 13194139534096 true] [17592186083789 1145 "The range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ consists of two intervals:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nWe can split this into two inequalities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\le -1,\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo find the range of $f(x),$ we consider both intervals separately.\n\n- Multiplying the first interval by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and subtracting $1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\le -1 \\\\  & \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\le -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})-1\\le -\\frac{1}{3}-1 \\\\  & f(x)\\le -\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Multiplying the second interval by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and subtracting $1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\ge 1 \\\\  & \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\ge \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{8})-1\\ge \\frac{1}{3}-1 \\\\  & f(x)\\ge -\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining both inequalities, we get\n\n$$\nf(x)\\le -\\frac{4}{3},\\,f(x)\\ge -\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the range is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{4}{3}]\\cup [-\\frac{2}{3},\\infty ).$" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277490 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277491 13194139534096 true] [17592186277490 1089 "q-66062" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277490 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534096 true] [17592186277490 1100 "Find the range of the function $f(x)=5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-3.$" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277490 1113 #uuid "f78b0f00-abf4-5ba2-a6f5-e47b01f3518d" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277490 1145 "The range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ consists of two intervals:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nWe can split this into two inequalities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\le -1,\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo find the range of $f(x),$ we consider both intervals separately.\n\n- Multiplying the first interval by $5$ and subtracting $3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\le -1 \\\\  & 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\le -5 \\\\  & 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-3\\le -5-3 \\\\  & f(x)\\le -8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Multiplying the second interval by $5$ and subtracting $3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\ge 1 \\\\  & 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\ge 5 \\\\  & 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-3\\ge 5-3 \\\\  & f(x)\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining both inequalities, we get\n\n$$\nf(x)\\le -8,\\,f(x)\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the range is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-8]\\cup [2,\\infty ).$" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277492 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277493 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277494 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277495 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277496 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1041 "selection" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277495 13194139534096 true] [17592186277491 1110 #uuid "b1674ac0-d8f5-5250-bd18-3da2707e75d4" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277492 1034 "f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [2,\\infty )" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277492 1111 #uuid "94056ffb-a25a-5ff5-bd39-f8615c37e2c3" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277493 1034 "f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{4}{5}]\\cup [2,\\infty )" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277493 1111 #uuid "b8eaf9c3-5baa-50a8-81be-e05759fa97a4" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277494 1034 "f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-8]\\cup [8,\\infty )" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277494 1111 #uuid "93784874-7b2f-5cbc-b194-9fadc3e5e3b4" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277495 1034 "f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-8]\\cup [2,\\infty )" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277495 1111 #uuid "b5f1aaa8-637f-504f-aece-60323fd2869b" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277496 1034 "f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-0]\\cup [1,\\infty )" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277496 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277496 1111 #uuid "ea7fbd0a-e4ca-5b8d-a277-dcb2c637ff82" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277497 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277498 13194139534096 true] [17592186277497 1089 "q-66071" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277497 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534096 true] [17592186277497 1100 "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534096 true] [17592186277497 1113 #uuid "24f4f8ab-4bd4-54bd-a8d1-e84a41a0a56a" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277497 1145 "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ consists of all values where $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\ne 0,$ and is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & \\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{6}+3n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{3n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+3n\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277499 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277500 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277501 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277502 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277503 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1041 "selection" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277502 13194139534096 true] [17592186277498 1110 #uuid "50ee9aac-3118-5863-b25a-cee61da864d7" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277499 1034 "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{5n\\pi }{2}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277499 1111 #uuid "1ca53a8a-1b88-5d73-92f7-c3a7d3a55291" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277500 1034 "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi " 13194139534096 true] [17592186277500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277500 1111 #uuid "1b5c154f-9bde-5c41-94d3-fd235425290b" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277501 1034 "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277501 1111 #uuid "b39457fc-d1b9-5ea2-bb3d-948b759c3a58" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277502 1034 "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{3n\\pi }{2}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277502 1111 #uuid "139cacce-77e7-5028-9844-38189882985f" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277503 1034 "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277503 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277503 1111 #uuid "29066276-cd13-57d1-ae56-f489abde8c63" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277504 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277505 13194139534096 true] [17592186277504 1089 "q-66074" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277504 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534096 true] [17592186277504 1100 "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x-{60}^{∘}),$ where $x$ is measured in degrees? Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534096 true] [17592186277504 1113 #uuid "5da223d5-ac9d-59a3-bcda-b66c2be933a1" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277504 1145 "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ consists of all values where $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\ne 0,$ and is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx\\ne {90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x-{60}^{∘}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x-{60}^{∘}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x-{60}^{∘}\\ne {90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-{60}^{∘} & \\ne {90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & \\ne {90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}+{60}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & \\ne {150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & \\ne {50}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne {50}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘},$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277506 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277507 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277508 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277509 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277510 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1041 "selection" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277508 13194139534096 true] [17592186277505 1110 #uuid "f182d070-f5e6-573f-8fb5-47eca6ca7fa2" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277506 1034 "x\\ne {50}^{∘}+n\\cdot {30}^{∘}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277506 1111 #uuid "1d4ba651-acd3-5302-b420-7cd5dac6e2c2" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277507 1034 "x\\ne {30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277507 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277507 1111 #uuid "a1fc413f-4e85-5cdc-abb5-65381d8df7fb" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277508 1034 "x\\ne {50}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277508 1111 #uuid "80fcdfd2-fb65-5a15-bda2-1e049725d4fe" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277509 1034 "x\\ne {90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277509 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277509 1111 #uuid "6cab8561-0644-5440-b8c1-2436e66c42f9" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277510 1034 "x\\ne {90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {30}^{∘}" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277510 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534096 true] [17592186277510 1111 #uuid "a5cb0a2b-5a99-5bd3-9ba9-28c4b1938fcd" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277511 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277512 13194139534096 true] [17592186277511 1089 "q-66087" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277511 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534096 true] [17592186277511 1100 "What is the value of $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+4$ at its local minimum points?" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277511 1113 #uuid "04a71c1a-0ab2-549e-ba81-a58fecdbea24" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277511 1145 "On a negative branch of the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\le -1.\n$$\n\nThe points where $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-1$ are **local maximums** of the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ For now, we're interested in the local maximums (not local minimums) of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ because we see that $f(x)$ contains a vertical reflection.\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\le -1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and adding $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\le -1 \\\\  & -2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\ge 2 \\\\  & -2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+4\\ge 2+4 \\\\  & -2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+4\\ge 6 \\\\  & f(x)\\ge 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=6$ at its local minimum points." 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277513 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277514 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277515 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277516 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277517 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1041 "selection" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277515 13194139534096 true] [17592186277512 1110 #uuid "5e90bbce-22bc-5a9c-9520-bfbfb49f5446" 13194139534096 true] [17592186277513 1034 "-5" 13194139534096 true] [17